+## Native delegated exchange
+
+The opt-in `request-exchange` build feature supplies the hosted startup boundary
+for a trusted sender. The library host sets `RunOptions::request_exchange`
+to its execution-bound sender and `RunOptions::request_exchange_pins` to trusted
+hostname/IP pairs before calling `strands_box::run`. A delegated hostname
+without a pin cannot connect; Box performs no delegated DNS lookup. Supplying pins
+without a sender refuses startup. That value
+reaches `HostedBox::open_with_request_exchange`, which uses the same
+policy, telemetry, and opened CA identity as ordinary startup, with an exclusive
+delegated gateway writer. Box credential routes are refused before resolution,
+and nonempty gateway credential capability sets are refused before startup.
+The sender runs as trusted code in the Box process, not in a separate sandbox. Ordinary `open` remains
+the default. There is no CLI or configuration switch for protected mode: a
+native Driver must first bind the sender to an admitted execution and its
+original response association. See the [gateway interface](../egress-gateway/README.md#delegated-exchange).
